 "meta": {
  "audience": "Age 5, just learning to read",
  "picturesPerGroup": 1,
  "grid": {"n": 3, "per": 3, "tiers": [1, 2, 3, 4]},
  "design_notes": [
    "Every word can be sounded out letter by letter: short vowels, plus the digraphs sh, ch, th, ck, ng and double letters ll, ss, ff. No silent e, no vowel teams, no r-controlled vowels, no tricky words such as was or the.",
    "Words whose vowel changes in NZ English (fast, bath, grass) are left out.",
    "Mostly 3 letters, some 4. Longer words are allowed only when they are easy to sound out, and tests/check_banks.py holds the list.",
    "Each word appears once in the whole bank, so clashesWith stays empty and a word can never appear twice in a puzzle.",
    "A 3 by 3 grid, because 16 words is too many to sound out. Each puzzle uses three of the four tiers at random, and three words from each group, so the lists hold more words than any one puzzle shows.",
    "The emoji array lists possible pictures. The generator keeps at most picturesPerGroup of the three drawn, so no more than half of the cards left on the board have a picture, however many groups are found. The cards with pictures change from puzzle to puzzle.",
    "Tier 1 is everyday things, tier 2 is less obvious things, tier 3 is doing and describing words, and tier 4 is word families."
  ],
  "tiers": {
   "1": "amber (everyday things)",
   "2": "coral (around us)",
   "3": "teal (doing and describing words)",
   "4": "navy (word families)"
  },
